	(text "Supplies (RP2350 datasheet): IOVDD, QSPI_IOVDD, USB_OTP_VDD, ADC_AVDD and VREG_VIN on 3V3 (the buck, power sheet);\nthe core regulator switches VREG_LX through 3.3 uH onto 1V1 (VREG_FB senses it), its analog supply VREG_AVDD\nthrough 27R / 4.7 uF.  Capacitors as Yannick placed them, each drawn at the pin it serves (C10 at QSPI_IOVDD and\nUSB_OTP_VDD; ADC_AVDD and USB_OTP_VDD have none of their own).  The RP2354A's 2 MB flash is in the package:\nits QSPI data and clock pins are not connected; QSPI_SS is the BOOTSEL strap (10k up).\nRP-BOOT (SW3) pulls it low through R11; so does Q3 when the S3 raises BOOTSEL_CTL (IO5).  RP-RUN (SW4) resets\nthe RP; so does Q4 when the S3 raises RUN_CTL (IO4): high = asserted (README: firmware).  USB: 27R at the RP,\nthe S3 is the host.  SWD and GND on bring-up pads (TP4, TP5, TP1)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 68.58 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd78b3c3-d57a-584c-992f-f458cb542276")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
